-- a molecule as the structured graph of its atoms: a type of atoms, each atom's element (its atomic
-- number) and each ordered pair's bond. No numbering of the atoms is part of the molecule, and that
-- is the content: the field's canonical strings choose one, and every automorphism below is a
-- numbering the molecule could equally have been given. The unchosen enumeration of §8.3 (a type
-- with ‖X ≃ Fin n‖) is the finiteness this adds to; it is not written here while the library's own
-- Trunc and Equiv are being rewritten (2026-11-18).
Mol : Type 1
Mol = (X : Type 0) × (X → Nat) × (X → X → Bond)
